From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:58:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dressing-room): lay out the Dressing Room around a skin
 preview

Rework the Dressing Room pages so they fit small GUI sizes and show
choices clearly, while keeping vanilla Java widgets.

A shared frame puts the page title in the top row between Back and
the Minecoin balance, and reserves two status lines above the footer,
so messages no longer overlap buttons. Chosen options use the vanilla
highlighted button sprite instead of the disabled one, which read as
unavailable.

The main page groups its actions beside a large 3D preview. Skin packs
and saved skins list every skin beside that preview, so one click
previews a skin and a double click wears it, instead of stepping
through one skin at a time. Owned packs gains a search bar.

The Character Creator keeps its tabs and slots in two rows. Slot labels
show the active and empty slots. The wardrobe lists all categories,
fills the space with a thumbnail grid that pages with the mouse wheel,
and shows piece details beside the grid on wide windows. Size and
color pickers use highlighted choices, and swatches are square and
mark the current color.

Saved skins no longer passes a missing skin to PlayerSkinWidget, which
crashed the client when the list was empty. A failed account character
now names the cause instead of only suggesting a retry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

